#: includes/abilities.php:743
msgid "True when the user making this request is exempt by role, meaning comments remain open for them even though the site disables them. Treat the other fields as the site configuration, not as what this user sees."
msgstr "Verdadeiro cando o usuario que fai esta solicitude está exento polo seu perfil, é dicir, os comentarios seguen abertos para el aínda que o sitio os desactive. Trata os outros campos como a configuración do sitio, non como o que ve este usuario."

#: includes/abilities.php:739
msgid "True when the site exempts one or more user roles from comment disabling."
msgstr "Verdadeiro cando o sitio exime un ou máis perfís de usuario da desactivación dos comentarios."

#: includes/abilities.php:735
msgid "True when the site blocks posting new comments over XML-RPC. Narrower than \"rest_api_comments_blocked\": only the \"wp.newComment\" method is removed, so reading and moderating comments over XML-RPC (\"wp.getComments\", \"wp.editComment\", \"wp.deleteComment\", \"wp.getCommentCount\" and similar) still work. Do not skip XML-RPC moderation because this is true. Independent of the post-type settings, like the REST setting."
msgstr "Verdadeiro cando o sitio bloquea a publicación de novos comentarios a través de XML-RPC. É máis limitado que \"rest_api_comments_blocked\": só se elimina o método \"wp.newComment\", polo que ler e moderar comentarios a través de XML-RPC (\"wp.getComments\", \"wp.editComment\", \"wp.deleteComment\", \"wp.getCommentCount\" e similares) segue funcionando. Non omitas a moderación por XML-RPC porque isto sexa verdadeiro. É independente dos axustes de tipo de contido, como o axuste de REST."

#: includes/abilities.php:731
msgid "True when the site blocks comment endpoints in the REST API, either through the dedicated REST setting or because comments are disabled everywhere. Non-allowlisted requests to /wp/v2/comments are rejected with a 403. This is not implied by the post-type fields — comments can be open on every post type while REST is blocked — so check it before reading or creating comments over REST. Types in \"allowed_comment_types\" are still permitted."
msgstr "Verdadeiro cando o sitio bloquea os endpoints de comentarios na API REST, ben mediante o axuste específico de REST ou porque os comentarios están desactivados en todas partes. As solicitudes a /wp/v2/comments que non están na lista de permitidos rexéitanse cun 403. Isto non se deduce dos campos de tipo de contido (os comentarios poden estar abertos en todos os tipos de contido mentres REST está bloqueada), así que compróbao antes de ler ou crear comentarios a través de REST. Os tipos de \"allowed_comment_types\" seguen permitíndose."

#: includes/abilities.php:727
msgid "True when a super admin has chosen to apply one set of settings to every site in the network."
msgstr "Verdadeiro cando un superadministrador elixiu aplicar un único conxunto de axustes a todos os sitios da rede."

#: includes/abilities.php:723
msgid "True when the plugin is activated network-wide on a multisite install."
msgstr "Verdadeiro cando o plugin está activado en toda a rede nunha instalación multisitio."

#: includes/abilities.php:719
msgid "Post type slugs on this site that support comments and can be toggled."
msgstr "Slugs dos tipos de contido deste sitio que admiten comentarios e se poden activar ou desactivar."

#: includes/abilities.php:714
msgid "Post type slugs that currently have comments disabled. When comments are disabled everywhere this lists every comment-capable post type, since the global setting also covers post types registered after the settings were saved."
msgstr "Slugs dos tipos de contido que teñen actualmente os comentarios desactivados. Cando os comentarios están desactivados en todas partes, isto lista todos os tipos de contido que admiten comentarios, xa que o axuste global tamén abrangue os tipos de contido rexistrados despois de gardar os axustes."

#: includes/abilities.php:704
msgid "Comment types that remain enabled even where comments are disabled, such as \"note\" for WordPress 6.9+ editor notes. These are preserved in comment queries and permitted through the REST API, so they can still be read and created."
msgstr "Tipos de comentarios que seguen activados mesmo onde os comentarios están desactivados, como \"note\" para as notas do editor de WordPress 6.9+. Consérvanse nas consultas de comentarios e permítense a través da API REST, polo que aínda se poden ler e crear."

#: includes/abilities.php:695
msgid "Summary of where comments are disabled: \"all\" (everywhere), \"none\" (nowhere), \"posts\", \"pages\", \"posts,pages\", \"multiple\" (several specific types), or a single custom post type slug. If \"excluded_for_current_user\" is true, comments are still open for the requesting user regardless of this value."
msgstr "Resumo de onde están desactivados os comentarios: \"all\" (en todas partes), \"none\" (en ningunha parte), \"posts\", \"pages\", \"posts,pages\", \"multiple\" (varios tipos específicos) ou o slug dun único tipo de contido personalizado. Se \"excluded_for_current_user\" é verdadeiro, os comentarios seguen abertos para o usuario que fai a solicitude independentemente deste valor."

#: includes/abilities.php:59
msgid "Reports where comments are currently disabled on this site: the overall status, which post types have comments turned off, and whether the setting applies across a multisite network. Use this to answer questions about whether comments are enabled before changing content or settings."
